mdl 1;
-- ============================================================================
-- mendixlabs/mxcli#1487 (ako/mxcli#1344): `marketplace update` writes the
-- package's manifest.json, License.txt and OSS readme into the app root
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Symptom, reported against v0.26.0 updating Nanoflow Commons 6.2.1 → 7.4.0:
--
--   the package's own metadata files end up in the **app root**:
--   - `manifest.json`
--   - `License.txt`
--   - `SiemensMendixNanoflowCommons__7.4.0__READMEOSS_<timestamp>.html`
--
--   Studio Pro does not put these in the project folder, so they show up as
--   untracked files. `marketplace install` had the same defect: both copy the
--   package's bundled files through InstallPackageFiles.
--
-- Root cause:
--   InstallPackageFiles copied every archive entry except project.mpr and
--   package.xml. package.xml's <files> list is what separates a package's
--   project files from its metadata, and nothing read it.
--
--   Measured with `mx module-import` on 11.12.1 (ExternalDatabaseConnector
--   6.3.0 and BusinessEvents 3.12.1 into a blank app): mx writes exactly the
--   listed files — none of License.txt, manifest.json, the READMEOSS report or
--   "Mendix EULA.docx" — and passes over a listed entry the archive lacks.
--
-- After fix: only listed files are installed; the rest are reported in one
-- line ("Left out N package file(s) package.xml does not list ...").
--
-- Usage (on a project with Nanoflow Commons installed from the marketplace):
--   mxcli marketplace update <content-id> -p app.mpr --to <version> --no-baseline
--   git status --short        # no License.txt / manifest.json / *READMEOSS*.html
--   mxcli exec mdl-examples/bug-tests/1487-marketplace-package-metadata-in-app-root.mdl -p app.mpr
-- ============================================================================

-- The model side of the update, unchanged by the fix: the module is present.
list modules;
